 @dechange4680  The power consumption is almost identical 170W vs. 180W TDP; that's a truly disappointing level of efficiency improvement for 5 years.  Of course it's entirely possible some boards use much higher TDPs, but you don't get a lot of performance from that (and undervolting hasn't really changed all that much either in all those years...).

For a sense of scale, remember that the 980 was released just a year earlier than the 1080, but the efficiency gain from 980->1080 was much, much better than 1080->3060 (or 3080 for that matter).

Mostly, GPUs have gotten bigger, hotter, and more expensive (and that's not only due to crypto, that's been the trend for years now), and only slightly more efficient.

